  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「チャンチンモドキ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%81%E3%83%A3%E3%83%B3%E3%83%81%E3%83%B3%E3%83%A2%E3%83%89%E3%82%AD",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106367084,
      "text": "チャンチンモドキ とは、ウルシ科の植物の一種。別名カナメノキ。センダン科のチャンチンに似ていることからチャンチンモドキの名がある。チャンチンモドキの花は赤褐色、チャンチンの花は白色ということで容易に判別できる。熊本県、鹿児島県、中国南部、東南アジア北部、ヒマラヤに分布する。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Choerospondias」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Choerospondias",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1375128364,
      "text": "Choerospondias axillaris, known in English as the Nepali hog plum, is a tree in the family Anacardiaceae. It is the sole species in genus Choerospondias. It is native to the central and eastern Himalayas in Nepal, Bhutan and northeastern India, and Indochina, southern and north-central China, Taiwan, and Japan. It is a common fruit in Nepal and Bhutan, which is called lapsi (लप्सी) in Nepali, aamli in Newar, and phrumchung in eastern Bhutan."
    }
  },
